    given-names: "Krishnanand"
  - family-names: "Agostino"
    given-names: "Christopher J."
title: "Deterministic Volumetric Auto-Rigging via Multi-View Orthographic Lifting of 2D Pose Landmarks"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-06
description: >-
  A deterministic, training-free pipeline that recovers a 14-joint
  humanoid skeleton from multi-view 2D pose detections. The pipeline
  rotates a mesh at eight viewing angles, detects landmarks with
  MediaPipe, inverts the observations with closed-form trigonometry,
  and anchors joints to the volumetric center via raycasting.
keywords:
  - auto-rigging
  - multi-view geometry
  - 2D pose estimation
  - skeletal animation
  - Cramér-Rao bound
  - volumetric raycasting
license: MIT
